WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.280
Tony Stark may be gone, but his genius&nbsp;
lives on through Peter Parker's suit choices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.160
in "Spider-Man: No Way Home." Peter sports&nbsp;
an outstanding number of Spider-Man suits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.200
throughout the film's 148-minute runtime.&nbsp;
Some of them are fits fans have seen before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.360
and others are brand new to the&nbsp;
MCU. Here's a quick rundown.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.600
WARNING. Major spoilers ahead.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.100
"You ready?"

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:23.600
"I'm ready."

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.120
"No Way Home" begins right where 2019's&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: Far From Home" left off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.840
Mysterio's doctored footage revealing the true&nbsp;
identity of Spider-Man is released by The Daily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.800
Bugle. Now, the whole world is against Peter&nbsp;
Parker and believes him to be a murderer. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.840
this turn of events, it's only appropriate that a&nbsp;
connection between the two films remains intact.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:48.400
This connective tissue is the very first&nbsp;
suit we see Spider-Man wear in "No Way Home":&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.880
his upgraded Spider-Man suit. The outfit&nbsp;
we see in the first act of the movie is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:57.120
the same one he creates on Tony Stark's&nbsp;
plane in "Far From Home" and proceeds to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:02.160
wear in his final battle against Mysterio.&nbsp;
It's nice to see this earlier suit return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.640
especially considering we've only seen it in&nbsp;
one previous fight. For the most part, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.520
older suit remains in Peter's closet throughout&nbsp;
much of the runtime of "No Way Home." After the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.320
opening sequence, Peter's in trouble with the&nbsp;
law, so he doesn't do a ton of crime fighting.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.160
The suit featured most prominently in&nbsp;
the marketing materials for "No Way Home"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.520
is the Iron Spider suit, also known as the Iron&nbsp;
Spider Armor. This is what Peter Parker wears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.240
during one of his battles against Doc Ock.&nbsp;
The Iron Spider suit is made up of nanotech,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:35.280
enveloping Peter right when he needs protection,&nbsp;
and boy, does he need it against the Doc.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.680
At one point during their fight, the scientist&nbsp;
takes a blade out from one of his tentacles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.400
Right when it's about to pierce&nbsp;
Spider-Man's exposed chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.160
the nanoparticles shift position&nbsp;
from his face to his chest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.560
protecting him from the attack while revealing&nbsp;
his identity to the multiversal villain.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.960
That's not the only significant development&nbsp;
provided by the nanotech. Otto Octavius&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.480
absorbs some of the particles into&nbsp;
his tentacles, providing them with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.720
red tint featured throughout the trailers.&nbsp;
Peter's able to use this to his advantage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:07.520
and since he has access to Tony Stark's tech,&nbsp;
he's able to manipulate the tentacles to do his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.640
bidding. It ends the fight and allows him to&nbsp;
bring Otto into Doctor Strange's holding cell.

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.800
When the first trailers for "No Way Home" were&nbsp;
released, there was a lot of speculation about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.520
what the black and gold suit would do. Was it&nbsp;
specifically designed to withstand attacks from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:26.560
Electro? As it turns out, it's simply Peter&nbsp;
Parker's upgraded suit turned inside out.

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.640
Earlier in the film, we see Peter get green&nbsp;
paint thrown on him. Plenty of New Yorkers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.520
believe The Daily Bugle's propaganda that he's&nbsp;
responsible for Mysterio's death. With no way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.160
prove his innocence, Peter has to put up with&nbsp;
various assaults, including being doused with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.800
paint while wearing his Spider-Man outfit.&nbsp;
He doesn't have time to get it cleaned, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.680
always wanting to look fresh, he turns it inside&nbsp;
out to deal with the next interdimensional threat.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.960
As it turns out, he looks pretty slick&nbsp;
in the new Spider-threads with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.440
prominent black fabric and gold accents.&nbsp;
Shortly after his battle with Electro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.120
Peter gets the suit cleaned, but&nbsp;
it looks great in the moment.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.440
NEXT up: This gold-trimmed suit is one&nbsp;
of the most highly anticipated Spidey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:07.040
suits fans have been waiting to see in&nbsp;
action. The design was initially teased&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.480
as part of a toy leak for "No Way&nbsp;
Home," and now that the movie's out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:15.200
audiences can see what the so-called "Iron&nbsp;
Spider Integration Suit" is all about.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.440
This shiny suit gives Peter the much-needed&nbsp;
boost in power he needs to take on all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.320
these previously-seen Spider-Man villains. And&nbsp;
surprisingly, it's actually in the movie for quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.120
a while. The suit first makes an appearance when&nbsp;
Spidey and friends are at Happy Hogan's condo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:32.960
He then takes the suit with him to the&nbsp;
final battle at the Statue of Liberty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:38.240
where he stands out compared to the suits worn by&nbsp;
Andrew Garfield and Tobey Maguire's Spider-Men.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:42.960
Yep, Garfield and Maguire both turn up in "No&nbsp;
Way Home." Merry Christmas, True Believers!

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:46.240
"Egg-shell-see-or!"

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.080
And finally … "No Way Home" has what&nbsp;
might just be the most devastating ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.800
of any MCU film so far. Before more&nbsp;
bad guys can break into their universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:59.520
Peter Parker has Doctor Strange perform a spell&nbsp;
to make the world forget that Peter Parker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.560
exists, but still remember&nbsp;
that there is a Spider-Man.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.960
As a result, M.J., Ned, and Happy will&nbsp;
lose all of their memories of him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.160
It's a poignant moment and one that exemplifies&nbsp;
what the Spider-Man persona is all about. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.120
entire philosophy centers around sacrificing what&nbsp;
he truly wants for the betterment of the world.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.840
The last time we see Peter, he has his own&nbsp;
apartment and is studying for the G.E.D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.920
However, he hasn't hung up his Spider-Man&nbsp;
suit just yet. He may no longer have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:29.840
access to all of Tony's gear, but he's&nbsp;
pretty proficient with a sewing machine.

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:33.600
The last sequence sees him jumping out&nbsp;
of his apartment window wearing a new,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.080
homemade suit he designed. We can't show it here,&nbsp;
but he's stuck with the red and blue palette from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:43.360
previous costumes, and it looks like he'll be&nbsp;
on his own in any future franchise installments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:47.280
Hey, the title wasn't lying when it&nbsp;
said there was "no way home" for Peter.

